{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Monitors source code files for changes and analyzes modified code for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, and best practices. Generates actionable suggestions for improving code quality while maintaining functionality.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "src/**/*.ts",
      "src/**/*.tsx",
      "src/**/*.js",
      "src/**/*.jsx",
      "*.ts",
      "*.tsx",
      "*.js",
      "*.jsx",
      "supabase/functions/**/*.ts"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code in the changed files for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any code smells like long functions, duplicate code, complex conditionals, or poor naming\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest appropriate design patterns that could improve the code structure\n3. **Best Practices**: Check adherence to React/TypeScript/JavaScript best practices\n4. **Performance**: Identify potential performance optimizations\n5. **Readability**: Suggest improvements for code clarity and maintainability\n6. **Type Safety**: For TypeScript files, ensure proper typing and suggest improvements\n\nFor each suggestion:\n- Explain WHY the change would be beneficial\n- Provide a concrete code example of the improvement\n- Prioritize suggestions by impact (High/Medium/Low)\n- Ensure suggestions maintain existing functionality\n\nConsider the project's tech stack: React 18 + TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, TanStack Query, and Supabase Edge Functions."
  }
}